# Binaries and test outputs
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
/alloca-go
/bin/
/dist/
/coverage/
coverage.out

# Delve debug binaries (e.g. cmd/alloca-go/__debug_bin*)
__debug_bin*

# Go workspace and local tooling
go.work
go.work.sum

# Local environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local

# Claude Code local configuration and sandbox artefacts
.claude/
.mcp.json

# IDE and editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Operating-system files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs and generated benchmark data
*.log
/tmp/

# Local load-harness output. A run worth keeping is promoted into
# docs/measurements/ deliberately; everything else is scratch, and leaving it in
# the repo root is how it ends up committed by accident.
/test/results/

# Observed run state: what was actually running, captured from the live system.
# The whole directory is ignored rather than one file at a time, because the
# reason applies to the class and not to deployment.json specifically — an
# observation committed goes stale silently and then misdescribes what was under
# test, while looking exactly as authoritative as a fresh one. That is the
# opposite of the *declared* documents in deploy/topology/, which are committed
# precisely because they state intent. Only the README explaining this is kept.
/test/observed/*
!/test/observed/README.md

# Terraform local state and plans
**/.terraform/*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# Local secrets
*.pem
*.key

# Discovered Prometheus scrape targets: a property of the machine, not the project.
/deploy/observability/targets/*.json
# Generated per-authority postgres exporter targets: a property of the rung being raised, derived
# from ITC_GROUPS by test/scripts/itc-obs-targets.sh, never edited by hand.
/deploy/observability/targets-postgres/*.json
